# Ratchet ceilings for the legacy SCREAMING_CASE arm of
# ci/test/css-token-resolution-guard.py. One line per compiled stylesheet.
#
# WHAT IS BEING COUNTED
# ---------------------
# Declarations in the COMPILED stylesheet whose value contains a bare
# SCREAMING_CASE identifier — a Stylus palette variable that did not resolve
# and that Stylus therefore emitted verbatim. No legal CSS value has that
# shape, so every one of these is a declaration the browser drops.
#
# They exist because `codetracer.styl` uses palette variables that not every
# palette defines. `default_dark_theme.styl` is missing 23 of them and
# `default_white_theme.styl` 34; the light build carries more because it is
# the younger palette. `BACKGROUND_NEIGHBOUR_COLOR`, for instance, is assigned
# in default_white_theme.styl and default_black_theme.styl and in neither of
# the two builds that ship it, so `#repl-history .repl-input-history` has no
# background in either.
#
# WHY A CEILING RATHER THAN A GATE
# --------------------------------
# Clearing these means choosing a colour for 57 surfaces, which is a different
# piece of work from installing the guard, and a guard that reddens CI on the
# day it lands is a guard that is disabled on the day it lands. So the number
# is recorded instead, and it only turns one way.
#
# THE RATCHET FAILS IN BOTH DIRECTIONS
# ------------------------------------
# Above the ceiling: a palette has lost a variable — fix the palette.
# Below the ceiling: lower the number here in the same commit that fixed the
# rule. A ceiling left above reality is room for a regression to hide in, and
# a stale ceiling is how a ratchet quietly becomes a rubber stamp.
#
# To retire this file entirely, clear the backlog and run with
# CT_CSS_TOKEN_ENFORCE_LEGACY=1.
#
# Measured on fix/unresolved-style-tokens off dev 558739ef3.

default_dark_theme_electron.css = 23
default_dark_theme_extension.css = 23
default_white_theme_electron.css = 34
loader.css = 0
subwindow.css = 0
